export const meta = {
  name: 'labmate-cockpit-live',
  description: 'Implement the cockpit live SSE view + session steering + report link, then adversarially verify build/integration',
  phases: [
    { title: 'Implement', detail: 'one implementer builds the live view + message-proxy route' },
    { title: 'Verify', detail: 'adversarial reviewers check build, SSE consumer, injection path' },
  ],
}

const repo = '/Users/vincent/Documents/code/Labmate/.claude/worktrees/resolve-spec-gaps'

const SSE_CONTRACT = `
The control plane exposes GET /api/studies/{id}/stream (public SSE) which proxies the agent runtime.
Each SSE frame is a single \`data: <json>\` line whose JSON has a \`kind\` discriminator. Emitted kinds
(from apps/agent-runtime/src/{server,loop}.mjs):
  - { kind:"session.created", study_id, session_id }
  - { kind:"user.message", study_id, text }            // the kickoff
  - { kind:"agent.activity", study_id, event }          // event.content is an array of {type:"text",text} blocks (agent.message/agent.thinking)
  - { kind:"tool.use", study_id, name, input }
  - { kind:"tool.result", study_id, name, result }      // result may carry {error, http_status} (e.g. 422 leakage, 402 approval)
  - { kind:"nudge", study_id }
  - { kind:"approval.needed", input, res }
  - { kind:"human.guidance", study_id, text }
  - { kind:"study.done", study_id }
  - { kind:"session.ended", study_id, event }
  - { kind:"loop.error", study_id, error, retry_status }
  - { kind:"loop.finished", study_id, sessionId, done, toolCalls }
When AGENT_RUNTIME_URL is unset (e.g. no runtime running), the WORKER instead sends a NAMED SSE event:
  \`event: info\\ndata: {"kind":"runtime_unavailable",...}\`  or  \`event: error\\ndata: {"kind":"runtime_unreachable",...}\`
So the EventSource consumer must handle BOTH default (onmessage) frames AND addEventListener('info'/'error') named events,
and render a clean "runtime not connected" state for runtime_unavailable rather than erroring.`

const impl = await agent(
  `You are implementing Stage 3 (cockpit live view + steering) of the Labmate E2E demo, working in the git worktree at ${repo} (your cwd is already there). Do NOT git commit — leave changes in the working tree.\n\n` +
  `GOAL (from docs/GOAL_E2E.md slice D + the /goal): on a live study, the cockpit (apps/cockpit, React + Vite + TS + TanStack Query) must:\n` +
  `  1. subscribe to the agent activity SSE stream and render a live activity timeline into the evidence-ledger area;\n` +
  `  2. have a working "suggest changes" box that INJECTS a user.message into the running Managed Agents session (not just a ledger note);\n` +
  `  3. update the run table as runs land (already polled) and show the final report + model link when the study is done.\n\n` +
  `READ FIRST (do not guess shapes): apps/cockpit/src/api/client.ts, apps/cockpit/src/api/hooks.ts, apps/cockpit/src/api/types.ts, ` +
  `apps/cockpit/src/components/StudyDetail.tsx, apps/cockpit/src/components/panes/EvidenceLedger.tsx, apps/cockpit/src/components/panes/Dock.tsx, ` +
  `apps/cockpit/src/components/panes/StatusStrip.tsx, apps/cockpit/src/state/overlay.tsx, apps/cockpit/src/lib/derive.ts, apps/cockpit/src/styles.css. ` +
  `Also read apps/web/src/worker.js (router + proxyAgentStream + triggerAgentStart near "agent runtime bridge"), apps/agent-runtime/src/server.mjs (the /agent/:id/message inject endpoint), and apps/api-spec/openapi.yaml.\n\n` +
  SSE_CONTRACT + `\n\n` +
  `IMPLEMENT exactly this, matching the codebase's existing style/aesthetic (glass-cockpit; reuse primitives, CSS vars, the toast + overlay patterns — do NOT restyle the app):\n` +
  `A. Control-plane message-injection route. In apps/web/src/worker.js add POST /api/studies/{id}/message (token-required write, alongside the other POST routes in the switch — note the router strips /api/studies/{id}/stream BEFORE the getStudyDetail catch-all, so handle the message route as a POST in the writes section by matching the path with a regex/startsWith since it has a path param) that proxies {text} to the agent runtime POST {AGENT_RUNTIME_URL}/agent/{id}/message and returns its JSON (or 503 {error:"runtime_unavailable"} when AGENT_RUNTIME_URL is unset). Add a triggerAgentMessage/proxy helper next to triggerAgentStart/proxyAgentStream. Document it in apps/api-spec/openapi.yaml as operationId suggestChange (POST, security internalToken, requestBody {text}) and regenerate packages/api-types/index.ts via \`npx --no-install openapi-typescript apps/api-spec/openapi.yaml -o packages/api-types/index.ts\`. CRITICAL: this must not break the contract test — it has hand-written per-op tests and no path-coverage assertion, but the router change must not disturb existing routes; keep createStudy/getStudy/stream working.\n` +
  `B. api client: add api.streamUrl(studyId) => \`\${API_BASE}/api/studies/\${id}/stream\` and api.suggestChange(studyId, text) => POST /api/studies/{id}/message.\n` +
  `C. A useAgentStream(studyId) hook (new file apps/cockpit/src/api/useAgentStream.ts) using EventSource on api.streamUrl: accumulate events into state (cap ~300), expose {events, status} where status reflects connected/runtime_unavailable/error. Handle default onmessage frames AND addEventListener('info'|'error'). Close on unmount. Reconnect on error with a bounded backoff. EventSource can't send auth headers — that's fine, the stream route is public.\n` +
  `D. Render a live "AGENT ACTIVITY" timeline (new component, e.g. apps/cockpit/src/components/panes/AgentActivity.tsx) showing the streamed events as a readable feed (agent narration text, tool.use as 🔧 name(args-preview), tool.result with a ⚠️ marker + the http_status when result.error/422/402, nudges, approvals, done). Mount it in StudyDetail.tsx within the evidence-ledger area (§04 region) for live studies; show a tidy "runtime not connected" state for runtime_unavailable. Invalidate/refetch the study query (qk.study) when a tool.result or study.done arrives so the run table + ledger update promptly.\n` +
